      "readmeHead": "# chat-demo\n\nEnglish | [简体中文](README.zh-CN.md)\n\nA static chat demo powered by the DeepSeek API. No application backend is required: the browser connects directly to the configured API service.\n\nYou can [try the app online](https://deepseek-ai.github.io/chat-demo/) or download the archive from [Releases](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-chat-demo/releases), extract it, and double-click `index.html` to use it locally without installation or a build. Enter your API key in Settings before your first chat.\n\n## Getting started\n\nInstall Node.js 22.12+ and pnpm, then run:\n\n```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/deepseek-ai/chat-demo.git\ncd chat-demo\npnpm install\npnpm dev\n```\n\nOpen http://localhost:8090.\n\nTo build the static site:\n\n```sh\npnpm build\n```\n\nThe output is written to `dist/`. Deploy it to a static web server or open `dist/index.html` directly. Opening the file directly requires browser support for storage on `file://` pages and an API service that permits their cross-origin requests.\n\n## Features\n\n- Multiple conversations with automatic titles, renaming, and deletion; edit prompts, regenerate replies, and switch between message branches.\n- Streaming replies, deep thinking, smart search, link reading, and source citations; stop generation or continue eligible replies.\n- Upload, paste, or drag and drop attachments; use voice input and read replies aloud. A live audio spectrum appears in the first row of the input area while recording on mobile.\n- Markdown, syntax highlighting, KaTeX math, and Mermaid diagrams.\n- Simplified Chinese and English, light and dark themes, mobile layouts, location settings, and chat history import and export.\n\n## Data and storage\n\nYour API key and settings are stored in the browser's localStorage. Conversations and original attachments are stored in IndexedDB. Local data is isolated by browser profile and site origin. Sending messages, uploading attachments, and using speech features sends the relevant content to the configured API serv",
